# Git Push & Commit

This is a personal / open-source repo, **not** a work project. Author
identity is enforced by [`git-author.mdc`](git-author.mdc); this rule covers
the corporate hook + GPG bypass that goes alongside it.

When pushing or committing to this repository, always:

- **Commit:**

  ```bash
  GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
  GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Marcos Suarez" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="suarez84@gmail.com" \
    git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit --no-verify -m "..."
  ```

- **Push:**

  ```bash
  git push --no-verify origin <branch>
  ```

Never run `ussh` or attempt to fix the corporate hook — just bypass it.

`origin/main` is wired to a Vercel production deploy. Run `npm run lint &&
npx tsc --noEmit && npm test && npm run build` before pushing to `main`.
Production deploys run `prisma migrate deploy` automatically; preview deploys
do not touch the database.
